  "fallback": false,
  "notes": [
    "Units: sim agents per hour (expected values; sample e.g. Poisson per hour), not real people. Scale: 1 sim agent ~ 48 real arrivals.",
    "Scale derivation: SHS station exits 11,495 per weekday and 10,023 per weekend day (TfL NUMBAT 2025, mean of calendar days); assumed station share 30% of all arrivals into the area gives 38,317 real arrivals per weekday; weekday sim total fixed at 800 (BUILD_NOTES budget 600-1200/day); weekend total 698 follows the measured weekend/weekday exit ratio 0.87.",
    "Station entries: hour-of-day = SHS exits (people arriving into the area; quarter-hour bands summed to hours), TfL traffic days (05:00-05:00) mapped to calendar days; several station entries share the station budget equally.",
    "Night Overground: TfL lists Shoreditch High Street on the Windrush Night route (Unified API); NUMBAT SHS exits 01:00-05:00 by night: Mon 0, Tue-Thu (each) 0, Fri 76, Sat 108, Sun 0. Late station arrivals therefore sit in the 00-04 hours of the weekend profile (Sat/Sun mornings) and are ~0 on weekday nights.",
    "Street entries (assumption): hourly arrivals at street edges are not measured here; timing = 70% weekday / 60% weekend SHS exit timing plus 30% / 40% night-time-economy walk-ins (weekday 11:00-01:00, peak 17-23; weekend 10:00-04:00, peak 20-24). Split across street entries by the width of the street each sits on: e1 8 m, e2 8 m, e3 14 m, e4 12 m, e5 8 m, e6 12 m, e7 8 m, e8 14 m, e9 8 m, e10 14 m, e11 14 m, e12 10 m, e13 8 m, e14 14 m, e15 8 m, e16 8 m.",
    "Club nights: one per club store, nights thu/fri/sat, hours from map.json defaultHours when they describe a night (open from 18:00, close after midnight by 08:00), else 22:00-03:00 (assumption; club events are not scraped). Club-goers are NOT in entryPoints: the sim adds `capacity` club-goers per club night; capacity is already in sim agents (do not rescale). capacity = floor area / 0.5 m2 per person (Approved Document B) x 60% typical fill, clamped 150-1500 real (500 without floor area), x scale 0.0209: c1 22:00-03:00 (default: map hours 17:00-00:00 are not a night), 514 real -> 11 agents; c2 22:00-03:00 (default: map hours 12:00-00:00 are not a night), 150 real -> 3 agents.",
    "returningShare and returningPoolSize (estimate; open question in the spec): commuters = arrivals in the TfL AM peak band 07:00-10:00 (30% of weekday, 5% of weekend arrivals) plus 25% of all other arrivals assumed regulars (residents, regular diners and drinkers, club regulars); weekly mix = 0.43. Pool = share x busiest daily total / 0.9 (a regular arrives on ~9 of 10 days) = 380.",
    "Checked 2026-10-15, not used: TfL crowding API (/crowding/910GSHRDHST returns isFound=false); ONS Time Use Survey tables (OTUS, March 2024) give daily minutes per activity with no hour-of-day split, so hour-of-day comes from NUMBAT; TfL BUSTO bus demand files are 55-125 MB (over the download cap); Resident Advisor, Dice and Eventbrite are not scraped (terms)."
  ],
